  "title": "Mausoleum of Caecilia Metella",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 43 C2 Sep. Caecilia Metella",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/tomb"
  ],
  "details": "<p>Map 43 of <em>The\u00a0</em><em>Barrington Atlas</em> labeled this feature with \"Sep. Caecilia Metella\"\u00a0and in the <em>Map-by-Map Directory</em> printed \"Cecilia Metella\" in the <strong>Modern Name / Location</strong> column.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A tomb on the Via Appia south of Rome belonging to Caecilia Metella, a daughter of Metellus Creticus. She was born ca. 100 BC. In 1303, the tomb was incorporated into the Castrum Caetani, serving as the main tower of the fortification.",
